@baseUrl = http://localhost:9001

# Generate a branded image for a Post — CON-105 (Nano Banana).
# POST /api/posts/:id/imagine creates a PENDING image Asset and enqueues async
# generation (River image_generate job), then returns 202 with the pending
# asset. Poll the asset until its status is "ready" (or "failed").
#
# All endpoints require authentication. Run "Login" from sessions/sessions.http
# first — the HTTP client stores and replays the cookie automatically.
#
# Availability:
#   - Returns 503 until a gemini_api_key is configured (secrets/secrets.http →
#     set GEMINI_API_KEY). The key is picked up live, no restart.
#   - v1 runs on the Gemini Developer API; EU-residency (Vertex) is CON-109.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   - {{campaignId}} set (run campaigns/campaigns.http → createCampaign)
#
# Sizing (§7): the aspect ratio defaults from the post's platform + post type
# (overridable via "aspectRatio"); resolution defaults to 1K. The worker
# validates the resolved size against the selected model and fails the asset
# (status "failed") if the ratio/resolution is unsupported — the POST itself
# still returns 202.
#
# Reference images (§6): "brandRefAssetIds" (style, ordered first) and
# "subjectAssetId" (content) are ids of IMAGE assets — e.g. a previously
# generated image (capture {{imagineAssetId}} below) or a brand asset flagged
# brand_style. Omit them for a prompt-only generation.

###
# ── Helper: a post to generate for ────────────────────────────────────────────
###

### Helper — create a draft post  [protected]
# @name createImaginePost
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "campaign_id": "{{campaignId}}",
  "platform_id": "rzgpTkARLH0L",
  "platform_post_type": "image-post",
  "title": "Post that needs a hero image",
  "status": "draft",
  "cta_type": "none"
}

> {% client.global.set("imaginePostId", response.body.id) %}

###
# ── Generate ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###

### 1. Prompt-only generation (aspect ratio from the platform)  [protected]
# → 202 { id, status: "pending", type: "IMG", ai_generated: true }
# Instagram image-post resolves to 4:5 by default; resolution defaults to 1K.
# @name imagine
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{imaginePostId}}/imagine
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subjectDesc": "a ceramic coffee mug on a light wooden table",
  "instruction": "warm morning light, minimalist, lots of negative space"
}

> {% client.global.set("imagineAssetId", response.body.id) %}

### 2. Poll the generated asset until ready  [protected]
# Repeat until status is "ready" (then `file.thumbnail_url` / the stored image
# is available) or "failed". Generation is async; premium can take many seconds.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{imagineAssetId}}

### 3. Explicit size override + premium (Pro) tier  [protected]
# 4K is Pro-only; the Pro model accepts it. Overrides the platform default.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{imaginePostId}}/imagine
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subjectDesc": "a hero product shot of noise-cancelling headphones",
  "instruction": "studio lighting on a seamless charcoal backdrop",
  "aspectRatio": "16:9",
  "resolution": "4K",
  "premium": true
}

### 4. With brand-kit + subject references  [protected]
# Brand refs supply the STYLE (ordered first, cacheable prefix); the subject
# supplies the CONTENT. Here we reuse the image generated in step 1 as the
# subject — swap in your own brand/subject image-asset ids.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{imaginePostId}}/imagine
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subjectDesc": "the same mug, re-styled for the brand",
  "instruction": "render the subject entirely in the brand's visual style",
  "aspectRatio": "1:1",
  "brandRefAssetIds": ["{{imagineAssetId}}"],
  "subjectAssetId": "{{imagineAssetId}}"
}

### 5. Draft-size override that the model rejects (async "failed")  [protected]
# 4K on the default (flash) tier is Pro-only. The POST returns 202, then the
# worker rejects the size and the asset lands status "failed" — poll it (as in
# step 2) to observe the terminal state.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{imaginePostId}}/imagine
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subjectDesc": "a wide banner illustration",
  "aspectRatio": "16:9",
  "resolution": "4K"
}

###
# ── Error cases ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###

### 6. Non-existent post (expects 404)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/nonexistent/imagine
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subjectDesc": "anything"
}

### 7. Unauthenticated (expects 401)
# Run without logging in (or after logout).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{imaginePostId}}/imagine
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subjectDesc": "anything"
}
